{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789263535,"nonce":"9wjIHn06BBLkwyYJkyXIumST1sY=","title":"A loop inside a block expression is lowered wrong or not at all","message":"`SsaBuilder::process_statement` handles statements that appear inside a\n`TypedExpression::Block` (an if-expression branch, a short-circuit\noperand, a lambda body) on demand, and that path is incomplete:\n\n1. `TypedStatement::For` has no arm; the loop is silently dropped and\n   the statements after it land in the same block. Loops at function\n   level are built by the CFG builder, which never sees an expression's\n   interior.\n2. `Break` and `Continue` have no arm either, so a `while true { ..\n   break }` inside a block expression never leaves.\n3. The on-demand `While` arm seals the header before the body is\n   processed and pushes the back-edge predecessor afterwards, so a\n   variable written in the body and read in the condition reads the\n   pre-loop value: `i = 0; while i \u003c n { i += 1 }` inside a block\n   expression spins forever.\n\nReproducer (Python frontend before 5b4a0c1 worked around it):\n`flag and len([x for x in xs]) \u003e 1` read the comprehension's list as\nempty; `flag and list(x for x in xs)` hung. Typed-AST shape: Binary(And,\nflag, Block[Let out = []; For i in 0..len { push }; Expression(out)]).\n\nThe frontend now emits an `if` statement assigning a temp instead of a\nblock expression whenever a branch has statements of its own, so no\nloop reaches this path from Python. ZynML's closures and if-expressions\nwith loops in their branches still can. Fix: give For, Break and\nContinue on-demand arms (a loop stack for the targets) and build loops\nwith the header unsealed until the latch is known, as the CFG builder\ndoes.","files":null}]}